# Send messages to the worker by hand (VS Code REST Client or Visual Studio), through RabbitMQ's management API.
# Start the stack first (F5, or the "deps: up" task). RabbitMQ management login: guest / guest.
#
# Rebus decides what a message is from its headers, so each request below sets them:
#   rbs2-msg-type      the .NET type name of the contract: "<full type name>, <assembly name>"
#   rbs2-content-type  how the body is serialized
#   rbs2-msg-id        any unique id
# The assembly name after the comma is the project name: change both parts if you rename the project.
@rabbit = http://localhost:15672
@auth = Basic Z3Vlc3Q6Z3Vlc3Q=

### COMMAND: send "import this order" straight to the worker's input queue ("worker").
# The default exchange (amq.default) routes by queue name. The orders API (http://localhost:5080) must be running.
POST {{rabbit}}/api/exchanges/%2F/amq.default/publish
Authorization: {{auth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "routing_key": "worker",
  "properties": {
    "delivery_mode": 2,
    "headers": {
      "rbs2-msg-type": "Company.Product.Worker.Handlers.Models.ImportOrderCommand, Company.Product.Worker",
      "rbs2-content-type": "application/json;charset=utf-8",
      "rbs2-msg-id": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111"
    }
  },
  "payload": "{\"reference\":\"B-3001\",\"customerName\":\"Northwind\",\"lines\":[{\"sku\":\"WIDGET-1\",\"quantity\":2,\"unitPrice\":25.00}]}",
  "payload_encoding": "string"
}

### COMMAND that fails validation: no lines. It lands in the "error" queue after ONE attempt (fail fast).
POST {{rabbit}}/api/exchanges/%2F/amq.default/publish
Authorization: {{auth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "routing_key": "worker",
  "properties": {
    "delivery_mode": 2,
    "headers": {
      "rbs2-msg-type": "Company.Product.Worker.Handlers.Models.ImportOrderCommand, Company.Product.Worker",
      "rbs2-content-type": "application/json;charset=utf-8",
      "rbs2-msg-id": "22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222"
    }
  },
  "payload": "{\"reference\":\"B-3002\",\"customerName\":\"\",\"lines\":[]}",
  "payload_encoding": "string"
}

### EVENT: the same OrderPlacedEvent a publisher would send, straight to the queue (an existing order id; unknown ids are logged and dropped).
POST {{rabbit}}/api/exchanges/%2F/amq.default/publish
Authorization: {{auth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "routing_key": "worker",
  "properties": {
    "delivery_mode": 2,
    "headers": {
      "rbs2-msg-type": "Company.Product.Worker.Handlers.Models.OrderPlacedEvent, Company.Product.Worker",
      "rbs2-content-type": "application/json;charset=utf-8",
      "rbs2-msg-id": "33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333"
    }
  },
  "payload": "{\"orderId\":\"0192f0a0-0000-7000-8000-000000000001\"}",
  "payload_encoding": "string"
}

### Health and metrics of the worker (F5 port)
GET http://localhost:5100/health

###
GET http://localhost:5100/metrics
